# Drafted by Gemini (R26 Tall Man), edited. The Tall Man: hook, clues, weakness, the lair fight and the aftermath.

~ arrive
set mf_tall_man_arrived
Narrator: A logging camp at the edge of a forest that has grown green and healed, the Wellspring bubbling clear, and every tree leaning slightly the same way.
check Wisdom DC 18 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ arrive_ok
Narrator: You keep to the lantern light and the whispers of the dark slide past.
set mf_tall_man_resisted
-> END

~ arrive_hit
Narrator: A heavy dread falls on a hero in the trees, their hands tremble, and for a long hour they can do nothing right.
damage 2d10 psychic party
-> END

~ region
Narrator: You walk the healed forest, and each tree you pass seems to have turned a little to watch you.
time +60
check Wisdom DC 18 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ hook
mf_bram_logger [afraid]: He says folk keep wandering into the trees at night in their sleepclothes, and the ones found come back screaming and cannot say why.
set mf_tall_man_asked
quest mf_tall_man asked
-> menu

~ hook_again
mf_bram_logger [weary]: He says two more went in last night, and asks if you have any answer.
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask what has been happening -> trouble
* Ask where it comes from -> where
* [if not flag.mf_tall_man_found] Ask how to find it -> route_a
* Say we will deal with it -> END

~ trouble
mf_bram_logger [afraid]: Each hour in the woods the dread gets worse, shadows stand up and walk, and voices call from where nobody is.
-> menu

~ where
mf_bram_logger [sad]: He says the forest was healed, green again, and then the moon shrieked and something tall came out of the old fey ruins in the heart of it.
-> menu

~ route_a
mf_bram_logger [neutral]: He says there is an old crone in the camp who tells tales of the Greenwood's court; her story might name it.
* [Arcana DC 18] Hear the crone's tale and test it against the lore -> a_ok | a_slow
* [Persuasion DC 18] Ask for the old court's story in careful words -> a_ok | a_slow
* Sit by her fire all night and let her talk it out -> a_slow
* Another time -> menu

~ a_ok
mf_bram_logger [smile]: The crone's tale is true enough to check: a graceful lord of the Greenwood, rotted by neglect into the Tall Man, walking his old palace's halls.
time +60
set mf_tall_man_found
set mf_tall_man_clue_a
quest mf_tall_man trail
-> menu

~ a_slow
Narrator: You sit through a rambling night of old women's stories, and somewhere near dawn she names the palace and the thing in it.
time +300
set mf_tall_man_found
quest mf_tall_man trail
-> menu

~ clue
mf_hesper_crone [sly]: She cackles that she has been telling this tale for sixty years and nobody listened until the moon fell on it.
set mf_tall_man_clue_met
-> clue_menu

~ clue_again
mf_hesper_crone [neutral]: A short greeting back, in character, that welcomes the heroes to ask again.
-> clue_menu

~ clue_menu
* Ask about it -> clue_talk
* [if not flag.mf_tall_man_found] Ask how to find it -> route_b
* [if flag.mf_tall_man_found and not flag.mf_tall_man_weak] Ask what could hurt it -> weak
* Take our leave -> END

~ clue_talk
mf_hesper_crone [sly]: She says the Tall Man was an archfey with a court of dancers, and he waits in the ruined palace, hungry for fear.
-> clue_menu

~ route_b
mf_hesper_crone [sly]: She says he comes to fear the way a moth comes to a candle; you could bait him and he would follow it to his palace.
* [Survival DC 18] Stalk the woods and lure him with fear -> b_ok | b_slow
* [Intimidation DC 18] Make yourselves loud with dread and be hunted -> b_ok | b_slow
* Walk the woods all night frightened on purpose -> b_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ b_ok
mf_hesper_crone [sly]: He comes, tall and long-limbed, and you lead him back toward his own palace walls, step by step.
time +60
set mf_tall_man_found
set mf_tall_man_clue_b
quest mf_tall_man trail
-> clue_menu

~ b_slow
Narrator: You blunder through the dark half the night before something tall finally follows your fear toward the palace.
time +300
set mf_tall_man_found
quest mf_tall_man trail
-> clue_menu

~ weak
mf_hesper_crone [sly]: She tells you the steps of the dance of his lost court; dance them in his sight and the old magic of the Greenwood hurts him.
* [Performance DC 20] Learn the steps of the lost court dance -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* [History DC 18] Study the old dance from her fingers' counting -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* Practise the steps clumsily until dawn -> weak_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ weak_ok
mf_hesper_crone [smile]: She taps the measure on her knee and you have it, six turns and a bow, a dance for a vanished court.
time +60
give mf_court_notes
set mf_tall_man_weak
quest mf_tall_man ready
-> clue_menu

~ weak_slow
Narrator: You stumble through the steps until the sun that is not there would have risen, and by then you have them.
time +300
give mf_court_notes
set mf_tall_man_weak
quest mf_tall_man ready
-> clue_menu

~ lair
Narrator: The ruined palace of the Greenwood court rises ahead, its pillars grey, its great hall open to the dark.
* Go in and face it -> fight
* Not yet -> END

~ fight
cutscene mf_tall_man_reveals
Narrator: The Tall Man unfolds from between the pillars, impossibly tall and thin, his head bowed under the roof he once was lord of.
cutscene mf_tall_man_reveals_2
Narrator: His long hand reaches, and the shadows around you stand up to follow it.
cutscene end
if flag.mf_tall_man_weak
combat mf_tall_man_weak
elif level >= 15
combat mf_tall_man_full
else
combat mf_tall_man_light
endif

~ aftermath
cutscene mf_tall_man_falls
Narrator: The Tall Man folds, his long limbs collapsing like a dropped puppet, and the shadows go back to being shadows.
cutscene mf_tall_man_falls_2
Narrator: The moon turns slowly northward, toward the Howlers and their snow.
cutscene end
set mf_tall_man_aftermath
set old_fears_slain += 1
set moonfall_credit += 1
set moonfall_nights_left += 1
give hook_of_the_tall_man
quest mf_tall_man slain
xp milestone
Narrator: High on the Howlers a rock slides, and something very large turns over in the dark.
-> END
